WEBVTT

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:09.420
I don't know anything about anything called the Splinter of Knowledge!

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.310
I know that.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.120
Then, why?!

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:18.090
Because you found out what I am searching for.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.890
That is your sin.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.070
I can't go back there. Not anymore...

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:01.740
You awake?

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.900
Hm? Y- Yes.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.030
Sorry, but I have a job for you.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.340
Can you get changed and come downstairs?

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.040
Sure.

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:12.450
A rush delivery?

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:13.510
You could say that.

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:16.720
Sorry to wake you up so early.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.880
That's all right. I'll be right back.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:38.470
Oh, hello, sir.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:39.640
Morning.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:41.440
You're certainly here early.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.580
Well, I have something to take care of.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.890
What's the big rush?

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:01.660
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:07.390
...the instant I look away.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:12.530
I just kept counting...

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:17.970
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:25.340
...that I'd vomited up.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:31.280
In this time that seems so dry,

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:36.390
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:42.250
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.300
...and tears them to pieces.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:54.970
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:02.800
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:27.650
What's the big idea, asking me to meet you in this dump?

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:30.890
For your sake, you better not try to foist off some useless info on me again.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:36.130
You have my word. Even a cheapskate like you will want to buy this.

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:39.650
You're a real flatterer. All right, I'll hear you out.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:46.430
A while back, the old lady who owned this area finally died.

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:51.770
Yeah, I heard about that. That old lady they said was immortal, right?

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.010
Yeah.

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:56.070
Is that the big news you said you had for me?

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.040
Give me a minute.

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:02.650
Then, how about the fact that in my circle, that old lady...

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:05.560
...was known as a bit of a walking encyclopedia?

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.590
More than "a bit," I'd say.

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:11.590
The way I hear it, there was nothing about Witches that she didn't know.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:15.100
Yeah, and the old lady apparently left behind...

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.970
...something called the Splinter of Knowledge when she died.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.930
Splinter of Knowledge? What's that?

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:28.110
Beats me. But rumor has it that Solomon is looking for it.

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:29.410
Solomon?!

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.620
You better not be making this up.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.880
I said it was a rumor, didn't I?

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:39.310
And if Solomon is after it...
Maybe it's information about Witches.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.860
If something like that were to fall into their hands,

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.550
...things could get ugly.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.830
See, didn't I tell you you'd be interested?

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.730
Fine. I'll buy it off you this time.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.610
But before I do, I want you to do a little work for me.

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:56.870
Like what?

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.610
I want you to find out where that "Splinter of Knowledge" thing is.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.280
Hey, wait a minute, that's a little...

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:07.090
Then we're through talking.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:09.380
You're not the only information dealer around here.

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:12.560
Wait a minute! All right, all right.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:17.150
Damn it, you're always pulling stuff like this, Nagira...

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:20.530
Splinter of Knowledge, huh?

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.800
That convenience store...

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:37.950
It was close to Touko's place.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.240
What are you doing?

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:04.540
- Well, if it isn't Lady Dojima.
- You're sure here early.

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:06.580
What were you checking out?

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:08.570
A murder.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:13.840
You know the Walled City, right?
We hunted a Witch there a while back.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:17.720
There's been a string of murders there lately.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:19.850
Of what, Witches?

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:23.750
One of the victims just happened to turn up on our list.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:26.090
So we started checking the others, and...

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:28.570
What, some of the other victims were also Witches?

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:30.400
Not some. ALL of them.

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:31.870
All of them?!

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:35.810
You make it sound like the Witches are fighting each other!

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:38.440
That's a pretty strong possibility, wouldn't you say?

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.640
The mailbox.

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:20.420
That letter...

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:28.660
The letter... How could I forget something so important?

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:43.400
I left it there.

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:47.240
It might be dangerous...

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:50.210
But...

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:26.920
It's gone?

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:33.080
What happened to it?

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:06.950
Other people are looking for it?

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:10.860
There's something seriously bad about this. I'd stay out of this if I were...

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.230
Who is it?!

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:14.030
You sure?

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:15.000
Start talking!

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:18.630
Okay, I'll tell you... The Professor, for one.

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:20.330
The Professor?

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:23.800
It looks like there are a few others besides him.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.510
So, it's not just Solomon...

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:30.280
Even a cautious guy like the Professor is making a move for this thing?

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:33.640
Whatever it is, it must be something major.

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:36.690
Come on, let's just call it quits.

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:39.620
There are even rumors that people have died for this...

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:43.090
Died? You mean people are killing each other?

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:45.630
There must be some infighting going on.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:50.230
Infighting? The way I hear it, the Professor works alone.

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:51.600
That's true, but...

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:54.310
In any case, I want you to keep digging.

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:55.470
But that isn't gonna be...

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:58.270
I'll make it worth your while.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.770
F-Fine.

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:03.270
See ya.

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:12.390
Michael, I read the report from this morning.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:19.600
Don't you think we should check into this case a bit...

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:20.960
I can hear you.

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:24.200
Oh, you mean the cases in the Walled City.

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:28.040
I think you're right. But isn't it dangerous to go there alone?

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:31.040
I'll just go there to get a feel for the situation.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:34.240
I see. In that case, I'll get the data to you right away.

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:35.810
I'll leave you to it.

00:10:45.590 --> 00:10:46.560
Oops!

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:01.130
The cops are on the move, too...

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:04.500
Looks like those rumors that people died are true.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:13.410
Professor, this isn't your style. Aren't you being a little reckless?

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:32.870
Yes?

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:35.030
It's me. Can I come in?

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:36.670
Oh, sure.

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:41.150
What is it?

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:43.640
There's something that I wanted to ask you.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:52.180
About a month and a half ago, an old lady died in the Walled City.

00:11:57.460 --> 00:12:00.450
I see... They had her flagged, just like I thought.

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:04.170
Nagira, how do you know about that old woman?

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:10.010
Well, there are these crazy rumors that she was immortal.

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:15.710
But even if it's a Witch we're talking about, I wouldn't believe stories like that.

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:19.020
But the real problem here is that "Splinter of Knowledge" thing...

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:22.180
...they say that this immortal Witch passed it on to someone before she died.

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.380
Splinter of Knowledge?

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:28.760
Right now, the Walled City is being turned upside down because of it.

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:32.350
Have you heard anything about this?

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:34.430
No, sorry...

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:38.730
Sworn to secrecy, huh?

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:41.830
The organization still has their claws in you, huh?

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:48.200
Oh, well. I can find out for myself even if you don't tell me.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:51.480
Sorry to bother you.

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:53.580
Why do you care about this, Nagira?

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.780
They say that Solomon is after it.

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:04.660
I can't just stand by and watch lots of people die for something like that.

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:23.610
The Splinter of Knowledge...

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:26.480
The inner mysteries of the Craft...

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:41.360
She knows something about this.

00:13:42.070 --> 00:13:45.500
This case might be even bigger than I imagined...

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:10.520
Oh, good morning.

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:12.230
Where's Nagira?

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:14.560
What's with the hairdo?

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:18.430
I'm not sure. I don't think he's in yet today.

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:24.970
Hey, where's Miho?

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:26.510
Beats me.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.600
She's out at the Walled City.

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:30.510
Walled City?

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:32.610
Oh, those murders?

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:33.780
Yeah.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:37.050
Don't you remember? We were talking about them yesterday.

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:40.890
Oh, you mean how Witches are fighting each other and...

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:42.090
Now look here...

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:45.090
But will she be okay by herself out there?

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.870
A guy who knows where to find the Splinter of Knowledge?

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:57.270
Yeah, that's right.

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:03.050
So... What happened to your face?

00:15:03.310 --> 00:15:04.870
Oh, this?

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:08.980
I had a little fight with the missus.

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:12.820
Anyway, what do you wanna do? You gonna see this guy?

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:21.260
All right. But if this is some cock and bull story, your face is gonna look even worse.

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:24.700
No way! I'm not making this up!

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:26.760
Give me a little credit, all right?

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:31.540
That's strange...

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:33.570
I can't get through.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:36.400
He usually checks in with me.

00:15:37.210 --> 00:15:40.510
I can find out for myself even if you don't tell me.

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:45.550
I can't just stand by and watch lots of people die for something like that.

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:49.190
I'll go look for him.

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:51.150
Look? Look where?

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:53.150
You know where he went?

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:57.360
Well... I'm not sure.

00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:00.460
But I'm sure I can find out.

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:04.170
Find out how?

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:11.770
This is the place?

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:16.240
I'm supposed to meet that guy here?

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:18.150
That's right.

00:16:22.430 --> 00:16:26.990
Professor... I see, so this was an invitation from you.

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:31.730
That little bastard...

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:34.700
I see you still have a sharp nose.

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:42.170
However, that doesn't seem to be the case where your own life is concerned.

00:16:56.730 --> 00:16:57.690
Michael...

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:00.200
Michael...

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:05.430
Are you up there, Michael?

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:07.770
Robin... Are you inside there?

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:10.740
Careful! Pretend like nothing is going on.

00:17:28.390 --> 00:17:31.120
What's the deal with this well?

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:34.550
More to the point, what have you been up to this past month?

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:38.340
I'm sorry. I was worried about all of you, but...

00:17:39.170 --> 00:17:40.500
I understand.

00:17:40.810 --> 00:17:43.710
Truth be told, though, I have no idea what's going on around here.

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:46.230
So, what do you want me to do?

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:49.710
You took a big risk coming here.

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:51.200
You want something from me, right?

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:56.680
The Walled City?

00:17:57.120 --> 00:18:00.830
That guy really went there to follow up on a hunch he had about the Witches?

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:01.690
Probably.

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:04.620
He might be in serious danger.

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:09.360
It looks like there's a war going on between the Witches there right now

00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:11.160
A war?

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:12.860
The inner mysteries...

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:16.630
Michael, is there anything you can do to find out where he is?

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:18.810
Easier said than done...

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:22.180
I'm sure he has his cell phone on him. If you can trace that...

00:18:22.850 --> 00:18:24.640
Well, I guess that's not impossible...

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:28.850
But that place is one big jumble of buildings...

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:32.060
If somebody could get one of our terminals close to him,

00:18:32.060 --> 00:18:34.350
...I could go through that, and...

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:36.820
Hey, that's right! Karasuma!

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:39.660
She's been there since this afternoon.

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:43.300
If I'm lucky, I might be able to use her terminal.

00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:45.500
Robin, what's that person's ID?

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:55.600
It's hot in here...

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:58.910
Think you could turn on the air conditioning for a bit?

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:02.480
You still love to hear yourself talk, I see.

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:07.120
I took the liberty of doing some digging.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:11.490
It seems that I was mistaken to think that you knew something about this.

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:14.690
You made me waste my precious time.

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:18.630
You fool...

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:28.470
A woman?

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:35.750
What?!

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:05.010
Nagira...!

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:18.690
That shouldn't have...

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:33.670
Hot!

00:20:34.010 --> 00:20:35.480
Oh, sorry.

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:36.410
That's okay.

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:43.810
Thanks for the help.

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:46.020
It was nothing.

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:51.990
Still, the powers of a hunter are pretty damn impressive.

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:57.230
That guy, the Professor, was the best there was in this neck of the woods.

00:20:57.800 --> 00:21:00.830
And you took him out without even breaking a sweat.

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:02.500
That's not true.

00:21:04.140 --> 00:21:06.510
That power wasn't what I had intended.

00:21:07.480 --> 00:21:09.610
I didn't mean to send out that much power.

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:14.080
The inner mysteries...?

00:21:17.350 --> 00:21:18.690
What's that?

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:23.020
This is the arcana of the Craft that I retrieved from the Methuselah...

00:21:23.830 --> 00:21:25.230
The inner mysteries of the Craft.

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:27.690
Inner mysteries of the Craft?

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:32.200
And I think it's also the Splinter of Knowledge.

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:33.190
What?!

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:36.470
Are you saying that you had it all along?!

00:21:37.210 --> 00:21:40.610
Dammit, what have I been doing...?

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:42.040
I'm sorry.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:48.150
Wait, if that secret is the Splinter of Knowledge he was looking for,

00:21:48.150 --> 00:21:49.880
...then your power just now...

00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:55.720
I see... So that's why they're willing to kill each other over a little stick.

00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:57.580
Solomon...

00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:02.500
Robin, something just occurred to me.

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:05.200
The reason you were attacked by those Solomon guys...

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:08.530
You don't suppose it was because of that thing, do you?

00:22:37.010 --> 00:22:45.000
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.820 --> 00:22:47.860
Tell me.

00:22:49.070 --> 00:22:59.850
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.710 --> 00:23:09.740
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.420 --> 00:23:14.230
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:19.600
...all those promises...

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:26.000
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:31.800
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:40.580
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
